From: RailgunHamster <railgunhamster@qq.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Apr 2026 22:03:10 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] debug: stub proxy test + lazy init + signature fixes
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

**Key finding from stub test (d3d12_stub.cpp):**
- Stub proxy (all forwarders return E_FAIL, no System32 load): game RUNS
- D3D12CreateDevice returns DXGI_ERROR_UNSUPPORTED → D3D11 fallback
- Streamline/DLSS crashes internally but game continues
- Proves the d3d12 proxy loading System32 d3d12 triggers the crash

**Changes in this commit:**
- D3D12CoreRegisterLayers signature fix (UINT→D3D12CORE_LAYERED_DEVICE_VERSION)
- Moved System32 d3d12 load from DllMain to lazy init (first FWD call)
  - Prevents D3D12Core init under loader lock
  - But crash still occurs (not the root cause)
- Crash callstack analysis: D3D12GetInterface+0x6F → D3D12Core ACCESS_VIOLATION
- Crash symptom consistent: writing NULL+9 in D3D12Core
- Three source code hypotheses addressed:
  1. Forwarder signature mismatch → fixed, not root cause
  2. Recursive LoadLibrary in DllMain → fixed (lazy init), not root cause
  3. Two d3d12 modules in process → ongoing investigation
